# Bench hardware status (current)

The Waveshare ESP32-P4 board under test is **not** fully instrumented yet. Treat missing
peripheral boards as **expected**, not regressions, until Cory confirms they are wired.

## Not connected (do not diagnose as failures)

- **RS485** — no relay board, no RTD Modbus boards. `RS485 * Online` OFF, Modbus
  timeouts / "Stop waiting for response", and probe-fault / fallback paths are
  **expected** on the bench.
- **External I2C temperature / humidity sensors** on the PH2.0 I2C header — not fitted.
  Missing ambient/external readings are **expected**.

## Connected / in scope for live checks

- On-board display, touch, Wi-Fi (C6), speaker path (ES8311 / PA), web/API — as already
  used in this project.
- On-board RTC (PCF8563) only after battery + chip are confirmed present; do not treat
  RTC FAIL as blocking if the CR2032 / chip is known absent.

## Rules for agents

1. Do **not** spend the session chasing Modbus offline / RTD offline / external I2C sensor
   absence unless the user says that hardware is now connected.
2. Do **not** recommend "fix RS485 wiring" as the next step for unrelated work.
3. When verifying control logic that needs temps/relays, say clearly that end-to-end
   coolroom control **cannot** be proven until RS485 (+ sensors) are attached; unit/UI
   paths may still be tested without them.
4. When the user reports peripherals are connected, update this rule (and
   `CLAUDE.md` / `reference/hardware_pins.md`) before treating those buses as live.
